            <ArticleTitle>Atrial myxoma mimicking systemic disease. Profile modified by flurbiprofen administration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1400-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient had a left atrial myxoma which was modified by flurbiprofen administration. The diagnosis was made 42 months after the first symptoms appeared. Flurbiprofen may have reduced interleukin-6 secretion by the tumor, leading to a delayed diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
